# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Krayin module skills — .gitignore
#
# This repository ships documentation and two Markdown skills. Nothing here is
# built, and nothing generated by *running* the skills belongs in it.
#
# The rules below fall into three groups:
#   1. Artifacts the skills produce when they run
#   2. Secrets and credentials — never committed, never published
#   3. Ordinary tooling, OS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Skill run artifacts — output, never source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# krayin-compat: the resume state file, written at the workspace root every time
# a gate changes state. It records the host app path and the module being worked
# on, so it is both noise and mildly sensitive.
.krayin-compat-state.json
.krayin-compat-state.*.json

# krayin-compat: the per-run output directory — a mirror of every modified module
# file plus CHANGES.md. It belongs to the module being fixed, not to this repo.
file-changes/
patches/

# krayin-blog: captured screenshots. These come from a real admin panel and can
# contain live CRM data, customer names, email addresses and phone numbers.
# Never commit them here.
blog-images/
blog-output/
screenshots/

# krayin-blog: the Module Analysis Notes doc and generated blog HTML
Module-Analysis-Notes*.md
module-analysis-notes*.md
*-blog.html
blog-*.html

# krayin-blog: the three verification scripts are documented inside SKILL.md and
# written out at run time. The copy in SKILL.md is the source of truth.
paragraph-check.py
image-width-check.py
image-order-check.py

# Seed files the blog skill writes to the scratchpad before capturing screenshots
seed-*.sql
seed-*.php


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Secrets and credentials — never commit, never publish
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json
auth.json
.npmrc
.netrc


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Tooling, OS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Node — the installer has zero dependencies, so node_modules only ever appears
# from a local `npm install`. package-lock.json IS committed on purpose.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/
*.tgz

# PHP — present only if someone runs the skills from inside a Krayin checkout
vendor/
composer.phar

# Python — the verification scripts run ad hoc; no cache belongs here
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Playwright — browser automation leftovers from a screenshot run
.playwright/
playwright-report/
test-results/
trace.zip

# Logs and temporary files
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/
scratchpad/

# Claude Code local state — machine-specific, not shared
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.credentials.json

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#

# Operating systems
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
